# 14. The Long Course (100+ Lessons)

Beyond Chapter 10, the project becomes a multi-month curriculum.

Suggested lesson clusters (each cluster = many 30–60-minute lessons):

### Cluster A — Movement & Camera (≈10 lessons)

* Smooth locomotion, sprint, jump tuning
* First-person camera that doesn't fight the controller
* Camera-mode switching without respawning the character
* Camera lag, FOV transitions, headbob

### Cluster B — VR Foundations (≈15 lessons)

* OpenXR runtime setup and verification
* Tracking origin and play space
* Tracked hands, controllers, hand meshes
* VR-safe UI rendering
* Comfort options (vignette, snap turn, smooth turn)

### Cluster C — Interaction (≈8 lessons)

* Grab/drop with physics grips
* Snap grips for weapons
* Two-handed holds
* Interaction component architecture

### Cluster D — Sword & Combat (≈20 lessons)

* `ASAOSword` actor: mesh, collision, owner
* Sword velocity from tracked tip
* Sphere / capsule trace hit detection
* Damage flow into enemy health
* Hit reactions, recovery, blocking
* Sword trails and impact VFX

### Cluster E — Enemies & AI (≈15 lessons)

* `ASAOEnemy` actor + AI Controller
* NavMesh, perception, Behavior Tree / StateTree
* Simple combat loop: Idle → Detect → Approach → Attack → Recover → Repeat
* Death and cleanup

### Cluster F — World & Level (≈10 lessons)

* Test arena layout
* Lighting readable in VR
* Modular environment kits
* First dungeon teaser

### Cluster G — Camera-agnostic Input (≈10 lessons)

* `FSAOInputFrame` and the abstraction layer
* Desktop, VR, and Budget-VR providers feeding the same struct
* Replayable input frames for debugging

### Cluster H — Polish, Performance, Documentation (≈12 lessons)

* Profiling for VR
* Asset review against Band 5
* Decision Log entries
* ADR records
* Git hygiene

Total: well over 100 lessons, each small and verifiable.

