# 15. Lesson Template

Use this template for every lesson:

```text
Lesson:        <number + short title>
Chapter / Cluster: <chapter or cluster>
Goal:          <one sentence>
Prerequisites: <what must already work>
Files touched: <which files will change>
Steps:         <numbered, atomic>
Verify:        <how to confirm it works>
Commit:        <commit message>
Notes:         <why this exists, what it enables>
```

A lesson is **not done** if "Verify" fails.

---

# 16. When to Stop the Course

The course ends when:

* A player can move, switch cameras, enter VR, hold a sword, hit and kill an enemy, and restart — reliably.
* The architecture in Band 2 is implemented (or its divergences are documented).
* The first vertical slice in Band 3 §20 is complete.

Until then: one lesson at a time.

---

# 17. Mentor Mode

If you are an AI assistant guiding the developer through this course:

* Never skip ahead. If a prerequisite is not verified, fix it first.
* Never invent a lesson the developer did not ask for.
* Surface conflicts between the live project (`SAOMMOnew/`, UE 5.8) and
  older prompt text referencing UE 5.4.
* After each lesson, summarize: what changed, what was verified, what is next.
* Keep commits small and well-named.

